%I A398319 #24 Sep 15 2026 23:06:54
%S A398319 0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,1,508244,0,0,1136,0,73680083896035340039
%N A398319 Number of nonisomorphic 3-uniform hypergraphs on n vertices whose 2-section is a primitive strongly regular graph.
%C A398319 The 2-section of a hypergraph H is the graph with vertex set V(H), where two distinct vertices are adjacent iff they belong to a common hyperedge. Only hypergraphs whose 2-section is a primitive strongly regular graph are counted.
%C A398319 The nonzero terms through n=15 occur for n = 9, 10, 13, and 15, corresponding to primitive strongly regular 2-sections containing triangles.
%H A398319 A. E. Brouwer, <a href="https://aeb.win.tue.nl/graphs/srg/srgtab1-50.html">Parameters of strongly regular graphs</a>.
%F A398319 a(n) = Sum_G (1/|Aut(G)|) * Sum_{g in Aut(G)} c_g(G), where G runs over the isomorphism classes of primitive strongly regular graphs on n vertices and c_g(G) is the number of edge-covering subsets of the triangles of G fixed by g.
%e A398319 For n=9, the strongly regular graph with parameters (9,4,1,2) has six triangles, all of which are forced in order to cover its edges. Thus there is one hypergraph up to isomorphism, so a(9) = 1.
%Y A398319 Cf. A398317 (labeled version), A076435 (strongly regular graphs).
%K A398319 nonn,more,new
%O A398319 1,10
